# Testing (derived from RAOS Ch.8–9, 16, 21)

## Prefer executable guards over prompt hope

- Place existence / Place ID validity
- Duplicate Place ID + alias
- Category purity (requested cafe ≠ bar)
- Meal timing / business hours
- Negative preferences (“不要火鍋”)
- Route fold-backs when planner claims optimization
- Membership permission boundaries (Plus-only modules)

## Levels

- Unit: Decision rules, validators, dedupe, category maps, credit/session helpers.
- Integration: Conversation → Context → Decision → Planner → Validator happy/fail paths.
- Contract: PIE/Recommendation inputs/outputs; domain schema version compatibility.
- Regression: previously failing place/category/hallucination cases become fixtures.

## Documentation

Important capabilities need design notes + data model + event flow + test strategy (`docs/raos/` + adjacent docs). Do not leave critical AI rules only in prompts.
